# From "Advanced Focus 10" (Wave I - Discovery, CD2-3): the shortcut version
# of relax-10, once the full ten-point count is already familiar. Also teaches
# a return trigger with a physical component (moving the right hand's
# fingers) that return-anchor.gws doesn't carry -- kept here rather than
# merged into it, since return-anchor is taught before this tool exists yet.

@segment   advanced-focus-10
@title     Advanced Focus 10 — Instant Access
@levels    F10
@duration  ~1m

# The tape pairs the number with a gesture -- "touch the fingers of your right
# hand to the back of your neck and repeat the number one". The gesture is
# dropped here, as it already is in `return-anchor`, because it is not what
# does the work: the owner reports returning on intent alone, sometimes
# without the number. Asking a still body to move its fingers adds a physical
# instruction to the one moment that needs none.
#
# The invitation to stretch and open the eyes belongs at the *end* of a
# session, in the return segments, where it is correctly placed.

say Once Focus 10 is familiar to you, you don't need the full count to return to it.
pause 5
say Inhale deeply. As you hold your breath, think the number ten, inside a bright, moving circle.
pause 6
say Exhale, and you'll be in Focus 10, just as you are right now.
pause 8
say Returning is just as quick. Think the number one, and intend to be awake.
pause 6
say Do this, and you'll be completely awake, both physically and mentally, refreshed, in every way.
pause 8
say The more you use these, the faster and more natural they'll become.
pause 6
